{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792041789,"nonce":"iC0FIqsTQAzfpYXfu/oHhbvv8Pc=","title":"Group headers carry a rule, titles are bold, links are faint, on every view kind","message":"Three visual changes to the view kinds (list, board, gantt, matrix), decided by the user:\n\n1. A group header carries its own divider: the label (bold, in the group colour as before), a space, then a faint rule of `─` to the window's edge. One helper, `groupHeader` in tui/render.go, draws it for all four; a nested list group's rule runs from after its indented label; the gantt's crosshair still runs through the header, rule included.\n2. An issue's title is bold wherever a view draws it: the list's title cell (bold under the wash and inside the reversed cursor cell), the board card's title lines, the gantt's label when the label is the title. Keyed on schema.TitleKey. Show is unchanged: it already bolds the title.\n3. A relation cell is faint, no longer underlined, on the list and the board: the issue it names is read on its own row, and the underline was noise. The reversed column-cursor cell is never faint, so the cursor reads the same on a link. Show keeps its underline (styleLink, its own code path).","files":null,"fields":{"area":["tui"],"parent":"2298f377f0e88711ec00d20aaa5922f7b11eab3053118c44d2fa445a71bdcf45","status":"in-progress","type":"task"}}]}